  ## in OLS, the fitted value Yihat = b0hat + b1hat * Xi is the models prediction of Y at Xi
  
### The OLS residual Ui hat equals Yi- Yihat, aka actual Y minus fitted Y
  
  ## a positive residual Uihat > 0 means the OLS underpredicted Yi
  
  ## R2 is the fraction of the sample variation in Y explained by X.
  
  ## Total sum of squares as SST= SSE + SSR
  
  ## The sum of OLS residuals is always 0.
  
  ## an R2 close to 0 means that the OLS explains little of the variation in Y, this is common and does not mean its a bad model
  
